                            <h2>What is Retro Bowl College?</h2>
                            <p>Retro Bowl College is a retro-styled American football simulation developed by New Star Games that puts you in charge of a collegiate football program. You serve as both head coach and offensive play caller, balancing on-field execution with roster recruiting and academic standards. The game captures the atmosphere of Saturday college football with classic pixel visuals and plays directly in your web browser with no download required.</p>
                            <p>Unlike professional football management where players sign long contracts, Retro Bowl College forces you to rebuild constantly due to four-year player eligibility limits. You must scout high school prospects, manage scholarship budgets, and keep student-athletes academically eligible while competing through conference schedules and bowl tournaments.</p>
                            <h2>Key features</h2>
                            <ul>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>Collegiate Roster Turnover:</strong> Players graduate after four seasons, requiring continuous recruiting and lineup adaptation.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>Academic Eligibility System:</strong> Student-athletes must maintain adequate grade point averages to remain active on game day.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>High School Recruiting:</strong> Spend scholarship funds and scouting credits to secure talented high school recruits each offseason.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>Dynamic Offensive Play:</strong> Call pass and run plays, read defensive coverage, and pass the football with precise touch or mouse aiming.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>Facility Upgrades:</strong> Invest coaching credits into training facilities, rehab centers, and stadium capacity to improve development and fan support.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>Postseason Tournaments:</strong> Compete in conference championships, historic bowl games, and the national playoff bracket.
                                </li>
