                            <h2>Recruiting and academic eligibility</h2>
                            <p>The central strategic challenge in Retro Bowl College revolves around student-athlete eligibility and roster management. Every player has a four-year clock covering their freshman, sophomore, junior, and senior seasons. Unlike professional franchises where veteran stars remain under multi-year contracts, college rosters experience regular graduation turnover. Coaches must identify upcoming departures and allocate recruiting resources accordingly.</p>
                            <p>Academic discipline plays an equally vital role. Players carry grade point averages that fluctuate based on team morale, study habits, and coaching intervention. If a student-athlete falls below academic standards, the program loses their services on game day. Managers must balance training intensity with study sessions or spend coaching credits on academic tutors to restore eligibility before critical conference matchups.</p>
                            <h2>Tips and strategy</h2>
                            <ul>
                                <li>
                                    <strong>Prioritize offensive line recruits:</strong> Giving your quarterback an extra second in the pocket dramatically reduces sacks and errant throws against aggressive blitzes.
